			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add async scheduling and network proxy interceptors to deep-shim system\n\nIntroduce two new proxy layers for Land's deep-shim interception architecture, completing Layers E (network) and F (async scheduling) alongside the existing EventInterceptor (Layer D).\n\n**AsyncProxy (Source/Shim/AsyncProxy.ts):** Monkeys all 8 async scheduling primitives — setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval, requestAnimationFrame, cancelAnimationFrame, requestIdleCallback, cancelIdleCallback — routing zero-delay timers through a microtask batch flush for coalescing, tracking interval handles through an ActiveIntervals map for proper cleanup, and delegating rAF/rIC to Land's render/idle cycle. String-eval callbacks are safely wrapped.\n\n**NetworkProxy (Source/Shim/NetworkProxy.ts):** Intercepts global fetch() and XMLHttpRequest to route network calls through Land's service tree. Microsoft telemetry endpoints (dc.services.visualstudio.com, vortex.data.microsoft.com) are silently discarded with a 204 response. vscode-file:// URIs are routed to Mountain's scheme handler (501 stub pending wire-up). Extension gallery queries (marketplace.visualstudio.com, open-vsx.org) are forwarded to Land's GalleryService (501 stub pending wire-up). All other traffic passes through to the original fetch/XHR unchanged.\n\n**FullIndex (Source/Shim/FullIndex.ts):** Combined barrel export re-exporting the core shim (Index.ts) plus EventInterceptor, NetworkProxy, and AsyncProxy — the \"everything\" entry point for the deep-shim system. All exports are dead-code-eliminated by esbuild when TierShim=None.\n\n**Documentation:** Add Shim Compatibility section to Architecture.md with shim tier comparison table. Add a standalone Repository README.md with the same tier table pointing to the architecture doc.\n\nAll three new modules are gated behind the IsEnabled check from Gate.ts — zero runtime overhead when TierShim=None.",
			"SHA": "bfefeb33a21df23add80241edb7ef02836ee103a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:26:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				806,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Install EventTarget.addEventListener interceptor for TierShim event swallow\n\nAdd `Source/Shim/EventInterceptor.ts` — a DOM-level interceptor that patches `EventTarget.prototype.addEventListener` to redirect matched event types to Land's RedirectBus instead of attaching them to the DOM element.\n\nWhen TierShim is \"Own\" or \"Preempt\", the interceptor checks each registered listener against SwallowMap rules. Matched listeners are registered on the RedirectBus (with the event type as the pattern) and the DOM attachment is skipped entirely. Unmatched event types pass through to the original `addEventListener` unchanged. The activation gate uses the esbuild-defined `__LandTier_Shim__` symbol in production builds, falling back to `process.env.TierShim` in dev.\n\nThe module must be installed at the top of Wind's bootstrap entry point, before any UI component registers listeners. This completes the DOM-intercept layer of the deep-shim architecture, giving Land control over event dispatch for specific event types that VS Code would otherwise capture.",
			"SHA": "072b495a2e9d70308841fee63f3192f86204515a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:19:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				805,
				23
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Prune orphaned Effect-TS imports from de-Effectified service domains\n\nRemove the final dangling Effect-TS import statements (Effect, Layer, Stream, Either, Context) from stub, mock, live, and layer files across seven service domains — Commands, Editor, Extensions, Output, Sandbox, Sidebar, and TextModelResolver — whose interfaces and implementations were already converted to native async/sync signatures in prior commits (f97e5dd, ae82728, ff60a11, 1621bf7).\n\nEach affected file carried an import for a type or function that no longer appeared in its active code paths:\n- Stub files (CommandsStub, OutputStub, TextModelResolverStub): strip the orphaned { Effect } import\n- Mock files (CommandsMock, ExtensionsMock, OutputMock, TextModelResolverMock): strip { Layer } import\n- Live implementations (OutputLive, TextModelResolverLive): strip { Effect, Layer } / { Effect } import\n- Layer composition files (Electron, Tauri, Test): strip { Layer } import from the top-level layer barrel\n- Interface files (OutputService, SandboxService, SidebarService): strip import type { Effect } / { Effect, Stream }\n- Problem type files (CommandsProblem, EditorProblem, ExtensionsProblem): strip import type { Effect }\n- Sandbox layer files (SandboxLive, SandboxMock): strip { Context, Effect, Layer } / { Effect, Layer }\n- Sidebar layer files (SidebarLive, SidebarMock): strip { Effect, Either, Layer, Stream } / { Effect, Layer, Stream }\n- Clipboard barrel: prune the now-unused Effect-related re-exports\n\nImpact: Zero dead Effect-TS import traces remain across all Wind service domains that have been fully migrated to native async/sync. This completes the import-level cleanup phase of the de-Effectification sweep.",
			"SHA": "6919b8dbc9868242e40d3a9cb176c1ad2a79551b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
