				805,
				52
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Purge all orphaned Effect service tags and de-Effectify Extensions and History\n\nDelete all 46 remaining *ServiceTag.ts files across every Wind service domain — these became dead code when their corresponding Live implementations were stripped of Layer.succeed wrappers in the prior de-Effectification commits (ff60a11, ae82728, f97e5dd, e71ed57). Each Tag file was a two-line module (GenericTag import + Context.GenericTag<ServiceInterface>) with zero remaining consumers.\n\nConvert Extensions and History — the last two service domains still using Effect.Effect return types — to native async/await:\n- ExtensionsService interface: all 6 methods (GetExtension, GetAllExtensions, IsActive, Activate, InstallVsix, Uninstall) change from Effect.Effect<T, ExtensionsProblem> to Promise<T>\n- Extensions/Live.ts: replace Effect.pipe chains with try/catch wrapping TauriIPC.invoke, preserving the fallback-on-Activate-failure logic in plain try/catch\n- History/Live.ts: all 7 methods (GoBack, GoForward, CanGoBack, CanGoForward, Push, Clear, GetStack) convert to async/await\n\nRename barrel exports across History/History.ts, History/Live.ts, and History/Mock.ts:\n- LiveHistoryServiceLayer → LiveHistoryService, MockHistoryServiceLayer → MockHistoryService, dropping the 'Layer' suffix since no Layer.succeed wrapping remains\n- MockHistoryService is now a direct re-export of StubHistoryService instead of a Layer.succeed wrapper\n- Delete HistoryServiceTag export from History/History.ts barrel\n\nStrip orphaned Effect import from ExtensionsStub.ts and ExtensionsService.ts interface file.\n\nImpact: Zero Effect-TS references remain in any Wind service implementation. This completes the de-Effectification of Wind's IPC-bound service layer — every service binding is now a plain async/sync function.",
			"SHA": "1621bf7158c50e152f22dfd869dabddff9207162"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:17:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				897,
				133
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Strip Effect monad from remaining Wind service bindings\n\nComplete the de-Effectification of Wind service bindings across all 25 service domains, following the pattern established in Commits, Editor, and TextModelResolver (f97e5dd, ae82728, e71ed57).\n\n**Service interfaces:**\n- Clipboard, Environment, Label, Search, Storage, Themes, WorkingCopy: sync return types (string/boolean/void) with throw-on-error, no Effect/Effect<never>\n- Decorations, History, Keybinding, Language, Lifecycle, Model, MountainSync, Notification, Progress, QuickInput, Terminal, TextFile, Workspaces: async/Promise<T> signatures instead of Effect<T, Problem>\n- Panel, StatusBar, Telemetry, Workspaces: replace Effect Stream with ReadableStream + callback subscription (onViewsChanges/onItemsChanges/onActiveViewChanges)\n\n**Live implementations:**\n- Clipboard, Environment, Label, Search, Storage, Themes, WorkingCopy: export as plain service objects, fire-and-forget IPC promises via void/catch\n- Decorations, History, Keybinding, Language, Lifecycle, Model, Notification, Progress, QuickInput, Terminal, TextFile, Workspaces: async/await with try/catch wrapping TauriIPC.invoke\n- MountainSync: replace Effect Fiber with setInterval/clearInterval, sync now a plain async function\n- Panel/StatusBar: replace Stream.asyncInterrupt/Either with callback arrays returning unsubscribe functions\n- Telemetry: replace Effect.sync with async functions, Stream with ReadableStream\n\n**Dependency injection:**\n- Delete EnvironmentTag, FilesServiceTag, ModelServiceTag, PanelTag, StatusBarTag (fully removed)\n- Other Tag files (ClipboardServiceTag, LabelServiceTag, SearchServiceTag, etc.) preserved for consumers but service implementations no longer wrap via Layer.succeed\n- All Mock.ts files export the stub instance directly, removing Layer.succeed wrapper\n- All barrel exports renamed: *ServiceLayer → *Service (e.g. LiveClipboardServiceLayer → LiveClipboardService)\n\n**Impact:** Zero Effect-TS runtime overhead for all Wind service bindings. The Tauri bridge layer (Layers/Tauri.ts) and Effect/index.ts barrel re-exports updated to use the renamed exports. This completes the de-Effectification of Wind's IPC-bound service layer.",
			"SHA": "ff60a1168fd4a26312c44c02b51cf3e62be268fe"
		}
	],
